# Standard Template
**MOST IMPORTANTLY** you **MUST** use fetch that is imported from [](../../../../src/_shared/lib/fetch.ts)
**DO NOT** use a fetch from any other library
**DO NOT** transform the return data from an API in any way. 
**ONLY** create functions that only call the api and return its response.

Also do not throw any errors as we don't want staging errors to be captured by our error tracking portal, we should only see live issues there

Use comment blocks to split each requirement to improve readability as per [HDFS](../../../../src/services/project-management/hdfs.ts)

## Request shape and return style (project-management style)

- **GET:** Accept a single typed **`params`** object. Destructure **path** segments the URL needs (e.g. `projectCode`), build the query string from the rest with **`urlParameterToString`**. Validate required fields at the top of the function.
- **POST / PUT / PATCH:** Pass the payload as **`body`** in the `fetch` options (plus `params` in the URL when needed).
- **Return** the **`fetch(...)` promise directly**—do **not** chain **`.then()` / `.catch()`** in the service to reshape data or swallow errors for “convenience” 
- On validation failure, call **`handleMissingParams`** from `src/_shared/utils/helpers.tsx` where appropriate, then **`return Promise.reject()`** (follow patterns in [milvus](../../../../src/services/project-management/milvus.ts), [kafka](../../../../src/services/project-management/kafka.ts), [starrocks](../../../../src/services/project-management/starrocks.ts)).

## GET
```ts
export const fetchClusterMetricList = (params?: IClusterMetricReq): Promise<IClusterMetricRsp> => {
  // Check if required fields exist first before calling API
  if (params?.id && params?.projectCode) {
    const extra = urlParameterToString(param);
    return fetch(`/api/endpoint` + extra);
  }

  const missingParams = [];
  for (const key in params) {
    if (params[key as keyof IMigDetailCancelBody] === undefined) {
      missingParams.push(key);
    }
  }

  // **DO NOT** throw errors 
  if (missingParams?.length > 0) console.log('Missing params: ' + missingParams?.join(', '));
  return Promise.reject();
};
```

## POST
Example with just a body
```ts
export const postEditClusterMetrics = (body?: IClusterMetricsBody): Promise<void> => {
  return fetch(`/api/endpoint`, {
    method: 'POST',
    body: body,
  });
};
```

Example with both body and request params
```ts
export const postEditClusterMetrics = (params?: IClusterMetricsReq ,body?: IClusterMetricsBody): Promise<void> => {
  // Check if required fields exist first before calling API
  if (params?.id && params?.projectCode) {
    const extra = urlParameterToString(param);
    return fetch(`/api/endpoint` + extra, {
      method: 'POST',
      body: body,
    });
  }

  const missingParams = [];
  for (const key in params) {
    if (params[key as keyof IMigDetailCancelBody] === undefined) {
      missingParams.push(key);
    }
  }

  // **DO NOT** throw errors 
  if (missingParams?.length > 0) console.log('Missing params: ' + missingParams?.join(', '));
  return Promise.reject();
};
```

## PUT
Similar to POST
```ts
export const putEditClusterMetrics = (body?: IClusterMetricsBody): Promise<void> => {
  return fetch(`/api/endpoint`, {
    method: 'PUT',
    body: body,
  });
};
```

## DELETE
Similar to POST
```ts
export const deleteEditClusterMetrics = (body?: IClusterMetricsBody): Promise<void> => {
  return fetch(`/api/endpoint`, {
    method: 'DELETE',
    body: body,
  });
};
```

# Variations
## rawResponse
An example from [Data_workspace_project_asset](../../../../src/services/data-workspace/my-asset/project-asset.ts)
```ts
export const deleteProjectMember = (body: ILeaveProjectBody): Promise<void> => {
  return fetch(
    '/project/member/leave',
    {
      method: 'DELETE',
      body,
    },
    { rawResponse: true }
  );
};
```
Use rawResponse when you need access to the status code of the API call (usually for rendering custom popups during code 200)

